surname><given-names>XD</given-names></name><name><surname>Goyal</surname><given-names>RK</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Nitric oxide involvement in the peptide VIP-associated inhibitory junction potential in the guinea-pig ileum.</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><volume>461</volume><fpage>485</fpage><lpage>99</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8102401</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004990-Mashimo1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mashimo</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>He</surname><given-names>XD</given-names></name><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name><name><surname>Fishman</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Goyal</surname><given-names>RK</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Neuronal constitutive nitric oxide synthase is involved in murine enteric inhibitory neurotransmission.</article-title><source>J Clin Invest</source><volume>98</volume><fpage>8</fpage><lpage>13</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8690808</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004990-Rao1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rao</surname><given-names>YM</given-names></name><name><surname>Chaudhury</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Goyal</surname><given-names>RK</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Active and inactive pools of nNOS in the nerve terminals in mouse gut: implications for nitrergic neurotransmission.</article-title><source>Am J Physiol Gastrointest Liver Physiol</source><volume>294</volume><fpage>G627</fpage><lpage>34</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18096606</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004990-Chaudhury1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cha